# Gym Management System — Day-by-Day Build Prompts

**How to use this:** Each day has a ready-to-paste prompt for Claude Code (or another AI coding
assistant). Paste one prompt per session, review/test the output, commit, then move to the next
day. Assumes Laravel 11 + Blade + Bootstrap 5 (matching the landing page already built) + MySQL.

Adjust package names (payment gateway, SMS provider) to your actual region/provider before use.

---

## WEEK 1 — Project Setup, Auth & Roles

### Day 1 — Project scaffold
```
Set up a fresh Laravel 11 project called "gym-management-system". Configure .env for MySQL,
install Laravel Breeze with Blade stack, and get the default auth scaffolding running.
Then replace the default Breeze login/register views with the custom dark+orange themed
login.blade.php and register.blade.php I already have (I'll paste them). Confirm the app
boots with `php artisan serve` and login/register work end-to-end.
```

### Day 2 — Roles & permissions
```
Install spatie/laravel-permission. Create these roles: super-admin, gym-owner, staff, trainer,
member. Create a seeder that sets up these roles and assigns super-admin to the first registered
user. Add middleware to protect route groups by role. Show me the migration, seeder, and
route group structure.
```

### Day 3 — Gym/Studio profile model
```
Create a Gym model and migration with fields: name, slug, logo, address, city, state, phone,
email, opening_hours (json), timezone, owner_id (FK to users), status (active/suspended).
Add a multi-step onboarding wizard (Blade + Bootstrap 5, matching my dark/orange theme) that
lets a new gym-owner create their gym profile right after signup: Step 1 basic info, Step 2
branding/logo upload, Step 3 opening hours, Step 4 confirm & finish.
```

### Day 4 — Base dashboard layout
```
Create a shared authenticated dashboard layout (resources/views/layouts/dashboard.blade.php)
with a collapsible sidebar (dark theme, orange active-state highlight) and topbar showing the
logged-in user's name/avatar and gym name. Sidebar links: Dashboard, Members, Plans, Classes,
Trainers, Payments, Reports, Settings. Make it responsive (sidebar collapses to icons on
tablet, off-canvas on mobile). Use the same CSS variables from my existing style.css.
```

### Day 5 — Member model foundation
```
Create a Member model + migration: name, email, phone, dob, gender, address, gym_id,
membership_plan_id (nullable FK), join_date, status (active/inactive/frozen), profile_photo.
Add a MemberController with index/create/store/edit/update/delete. Build the "Members" list
page in the dashboard layout: searchable/sortable table (DataTables or simple Bootstrap table
with search input), status badges (green=active/orange=expiring soon/red=expired).
```

