## WEEK 2 — Membership Plans & Subscriptions

### Day 6 — Membership plans CRUD
```
Create a MembershipPlan model + migration: name, price, duration_days, description,
features (json array), is_active. Build full CRUD in the dashboard: a "Plans" page with
pricing-card-style previews (reuse the pricing-card component style from my landing page,
but functional with edit/delete buttons for gym-owner role only).
```

### Day 7 — Subscription/assignment logic
```
Create a Subscription model + migration linking member_id, plan_id, start_date, end_date,
amount_paid, status (active/expired/cancelled). Add logic so when a plan is assigned to a
member, end_date is auto-calculated from plan duration. Add an "Assign Plan" button on the
member detail page that opens a modal to select a plan and confirm.
```

### Day 8 — Member detail page
```
Build a Member Profile page showing: personal info, current subscription with days remaining
(progress bar styled like the site's orange accent), subscription history table, and quick
action buttons: Renew, Freeze, Cancel, Edit.
```

### Day 9 — Expiry status automation
```
Create a scheduled Artisan command (php artisan memberships:check-expiry) that runs daily via
the Laravel scheduler, marks subscriptions as 'expired' when end_date has passed, and flags
members whose plan expires within 3 days as 'expiring soon'. Add a dashboard widget showing
counts: Active, Expiring in 3 days, Expired this week.
```

### Day 10 — Dashboard analytics v1
```
Build the main admin Dashboard home page with 4 stat cards (Total Members, Active
Subscriptions, Revenue This Month, Expiring This Week) styled like the pricing cards
(dark surface, orange icon accents), plus a simple line chart (Chart.js) showing new
member sign-ups over the last 30 days.
```

