## WEEK 4 — Class Booking System

### Day 16 — Class & schedule models
```
Create GymClass model (name, description, trainer_id, capacity, duration_minutes) and
ClassSchedule model (class_id, day_of_week or specific_date, start_time, recurring bool).
Build admin CRUD pages to create classes and set weekly recurring schedules.
```

### Day 17 — Member-facing class calendar
```
Build a member-facing "Book a Class" page showing a weekly calendar view (styled with the
dark/orange theme) of available class slots, seats remaining per slot, and a Book button.
Prevent booking if capacity is full — show "Join Waitlist" instead.
```

### Day 18 — Booking logic & waitlist
```
Create a ClassBooking model (member_id, schedule_id, status: booked/waitlisted/cancelled/
attended). Implement booking logic: capacity check, auto-promote first waitlisted member
when someone cancels, and prevent double-booking the same slot.
```

### Day 19 — Booking notifications
```
Send an email (and prepare a stub for WhatsApp/SMS via a NotificationService interface) when:
a booking is confirmed, a member is promoted from waitlist, or a class is cancelled by admin.
Use Laravel Notifications for this.
```

### Day 20 — Admin class roster & check-in
```
Build an admin page per class session showing the roster of booked members with a "Mark
Attended" checkbox for each, and a live seats-remaining counter. Add a simple QR-code
check-in option: generate a QR per member that staff can scan to mark attendance.
```

