## WEEK 5 — Trainer Booking & Attendance

### Day 21 — Trainer profiles
```
Create Trainer model (linked to a user with 'trainer' role): bio, specialties (json),
certifications, profile_photo, hourly_rate. Build a public Trainer directory page (reusing
the site's trainer-profile card style) and an admin CRUD for managing trainers.
```

### Day 22 — Trainer availability
```
Create a TrainerAvailability model (trainer_id, day_of_week, start_time, end_time). Build a
trainer-facing "My Availability" page where trainers set their own weekly working hours.
```

### Day 23 — Personal training booking flow
```
Build a member-facing "Book a Trainer" flow: pick trainer -> pick available date/time slot
(computed from TrainerAvailability minus existing bookings) -> confirm booking. Create a
PTBooking model (member_id, trainer_id, date, start_time, end_time, status).
```

### Day 24 — General attendance/check-in
```
Add a gym-wide check-in system independent of classes: each member gets a QR code (shown on
their profile / emailed), front-desk staff have a "Check-In" scanner page (can use a simple
webcam-based QR scanner JS library), and each check-in logs a timestamp to an Attendance
table.
```

### Day 25 — Attendance reports
```
Build a Reports > Attendance page: daily footfall chart (last 30 days), busiest hours
heatmap, and per-member attendance history (useful for gym owners to spot inactive members
at risk of churn).
```

