## WEEK 6 — Renewals, Polish & Launch Prep

### Day 26 — Automated renewal reminders
```
Extend the memberships:check-expiry scheduled command to send renewal reminder emails at
7 days, 3 days, and 1 day before expiry, plus an "expired" notice. Make templates match the
site's branding. Add an unsubscribe/preferences toggle per member.
```

### Day 27 — Role-based permission audit
```
Go through every route and controller and verify role-based access is correctly enforced
(a trainer shouldn't see billing, a member shouldn't see other members' data, staff shouldn't
access owner-only settings). Write a checklist of what you tested and flag any gaps found.
```

### Day 28 — Settings & gym customization
```
Build a Settings page for gym-owners: update gym profile/branding, manage staff accounts
(invite staff by email with role assignment), configure notification preferences, and manage
payment gateway keys per gym (if multi-tenant).
```

### Day 29 — Testing pass
```
Write PHPUnit/Pest feature tests covering: registration, login, plan assignment, subscription
expiry logic, class booking capacity limits, and payment webhook handling. Fix any bugs
found.
```

### Day 30 — Deployment prep
```
Prepare the app for production: set up .env.production template, configure queue worker for
notifications, set up the Laravel scheduler (cron), add error monitoring (e.g. Sentry stub),
and write a DEPLOYMENT.md with step-by-step server setup instructions (PHP version, extensions,
composer install --no-dev, migrate --force, storage link, queue:work supervisor config).
```

