## Phase 4 — Scale (Weekly prompts, Weeks 11–16+)

### Week 11–12 — Multi-branch support
```
Refactor the schema to properly support multi-branch gyms: add a Branch model under Gym,
move Members/Classes/Trainers to be branch-scoped, and add a branch switcher in the
dashboard for owners managing multiple locations. Add branch-level reporting.
```

### Week 13 — Advanced analytics
```
Build an analytics v2 dashboard: churn rate calculation, revenue trends with month-over-month
comparison, trainer performance (sessions booked, ratings), and class utilization rates
(booked vs capacity over time).
```

### Week 14–16 — Mobile app foundation
```
Set up a Flutter (or React Native) mobile app project that consumes the Laravel backend via
a versioned REST API (Laravel Sanctum for token auth). Start with: login/register, view
membership status, book a class, and view workout plan — the four highest-usage screens.
```

### Ongoing — White-label / marketing tie-in
```
Add a "branding" settings tab so gym-owners on a higher-tier plan can customize their member
portal's colors/logo. Connect the public landing page contact form to auto-create a lead in
a simple CRM table, and add an admin "Leads" page for the Gym Website Builder sales team to
track inquiries from the marketing site into paying gym-management customers.
```

